# JS/TS release (Changesets, commit-driven)

The npm packages in the bun workspace (`node/*`) release via
[Changesets](https://changesets.dev), the JS counterpart to `release-plz` for the
Rust crates. It is driven **automatically from conventional commits** — you
normally do not write changeset files by hand.

## Default: rely on conventional commits

On every push to `main`, [`js-changeset-autogen`](../../.github/workflows/js-changeset-autogen.yaml)
runs [`scripts/autogen-changeset.ts`](../../scripts/autogen-changeset.ts) over the
commits that touched `node/**` and generates the `.changeset/*.md` entries from the
`type(scope):` prefix:

| Commit type | Bump  |
|-------------|-------|
| `feat`      | minor |
| `fix` / `perf` / `refactor` | patch |
| `!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer | major |
| `chore` / `docs` / `test` / `ci` / `build` | none (no release) |

The **`(scope)`** is matched to a package by its directory basename, its unscoped
npm name, or its full name (e.g. `feat(editor):` → `@open-lakehouse/editor`;
`fix(client):` → `@unitycatalog/client`). A comma-separated scope
(`feat(query,editor):`) bumps both. A commit with **no scope**, or a scope that
matches no package, is skipped — so **scope your `node/` commits** if you want them
to release.

So a normal PR needs **no** changeset file: just use a correctly-scoped
conventional commit (the same commits already feed release-plz on the Rust side).

## Hand-write a changeset when the automatic mapping is wrong

Run `bun run changeset` and commit the generated `.changeset/*.md` when:

- a change is **breaking** and needs an explicit `major` + migration note in the
  release notes;
- a package needs a **different bump** than its commit type implies;
- the change is **cross-cutting** and you want to author the release-note summary.

Format (frontmatter = package → bump, body = the changelog line):

```markdown
---
"@unitycatalog/client": major
---

Rename `Client.connect()` → `Client.open()`. Update call sites accordingly.
```

A hand-written changeset **wins**: `changeset version` merges the manual and
autogenerated entries by taking the highest bump per package, so adding one is
always safe.

## Publishing is currently DORMANT (dry-run)

[`js-release`](../../.github/workflows/js-release.yaml) opens a "Version Packages"
PR from accumulated changesets; merging it bumps versions + writes CHANGELOGs.
The publish job runs **`--dry-run` only** and does **not** push to npm while the
`JS_PUBLISH_ENABLED` repo variable is unset or not `"true"`. Only
`@unitycatalog/client` (+ its platform packages) is non-private today; every
`@open-lakehouse/*` package is `private: true` and Changesets skips it. The
publish scope is decided in a follow-up.

## Notes

- Adding JS deps touches `bun.lock` — still run `bun run strip-lock-proxy` +
  `strip-lock-proxy:check` before a PR (see the bun.lock rule).
- `.changeset/` lives at the repo root, so changeset commits do **not** trigger
  the `just ui-fingerprint` (`crates/server/ui.lock`) path.
- Keep the commit-message contract (conventional `type(scope):`,
  `AI-assisted-by: Isaac`) — it feeds both this pipeline and release-plz.
